# ConferAtlas runs as two apps, each with its own settings file:
#   backend/.env   model keys, data folder, API token     (copy backend/.env.example)
#   frontend/.env  backend URL, API token, staff sign-in  (copy frontend/.env.example)
# The backend still reads a .env here as a fallback, so an older single-app setup keeps working.
#
# Docker Compose reads this root .env for the shared token it passes to both containers:
# BACKEND_API_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
